Z||000000||87ECO5||04-17-2000||09:23 AM||||Ran a search against the database.  Found several threads that talked about the modified shifter but none of them discussed the steps to install them.<P>Can someone help here?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||HF6582||04-17-2000||11:33 AM||||87,<BR>They are real easy. Just take the shift console surround piece off, then thake the shift cable off the shift arm, then pull the E clip that holds the arm on. Install the new arm and just reverse the steps now.<P><BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000002||BBBAD GT||04-17-2000||01:03 PM||||I would definately do it.  I couldn't believe how the stock shifter was, almost hitting the roof with every shift  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I bought one of Rodney Dickman's comp short shifter, and I'm very happy with it.  I does make a world of difference, at least to me it did.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bruce||04-18-2000||01:12 AM||||Look-up TOM through the forum, relative to short shifters. He includes, or did, the shift knob. It's about $25. I still don't know if "short throw" applies to Tom's or Rodney's. But, I keep everything as simple as oil changes and such.<BR>bb||||reg||1
